      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Ranchos%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Rancho Los Cerritos, a public museum built in 1844, showcases adobe architecture that reflects Spanish, Mexican, and early American California.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.americanheritage.com/content/ranchos-los-cerritos",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The museum grounds feature gardens that honor Gabrielino‑Tongva ancestry, offering a living glimpse into California’s indigenous heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rancholoscerritos.org/homepage-2/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rancho Los Cerritos hosts rotating exhibits that invite visitors to reconsider what defines American history, including a focus on women of Barrio Americano.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rancholoscerritos.org/homepage-2/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The site is recognized as a National, State, and Long Beach Historic Landmark, preserving both its gardens and research library for future generations.",
